--- a top-level variable's first assignment is judged against nothing: an
--- earlier round had read a mask of a function's answer as one number
--- (before the function was typed), and the one assignment the variable
--- has was refused as a reassignment (Rosetta Code, Statistics/Normal
--- distribution)

fn half[x]
    return x / 2.0

z = [1.0, -2.0, 3.0]
inside = z[z lt half[1.0]]
log[inside]
m = z gt half[1.0]
picked = z[m]
log[picked]
